00:16:35.629 --> 00:16:37.700
So we can always go back here

00:16:43.249 --> 00:16:44.150
if we needed to.

00:16:44.720 --> 00:16:50.900
Now, in order to connect pH and
POH, we can do that as well.

00:16:51.749 --> 00:16:56.510
So we can always have an
equation between both of these.

00:16:57.520 --> 00:17:03.979
So if we want to go to POH,
that was simply, uh, pH plus.

00:17:05.244 --> 00:17:09.774
the pOH is equal to 14.

00:17:10.324 --> 00:17:13.365
So you can bridge
between those two values.

00:17:14.254 --> 00:17:20.904
Now if we wanted to do our last one, let's
say if we had hydroxide here, we can also

00:17:20.915 --> 00:17:23.405
bridge the gap between these as well.

00:17:24.054 --> 00:17:28.754
So if I want to go to hydroxide, we
could once again take the 10 to the

00:17:28.764 --> 00:17:35.514
negative pOH to go over to hydroxide.

00:17:37.245 --> 00:17:42.570
Or if we wanted to convert, Back
to pH, we could find the negative

00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:46.669
log of OH to convert back.

00:17:47.220 --> 00:17:48.120
So it's a cycle.

00:17:48.530 --> 00:17:49.850
So how do we connect the last one?

